# Web app settings — copy to `apps/web/.env` and fill in.
#
# These are separate from the root `.env` on purpose: only variables prefixed
# with VITE_ are exposed to the browser bundle, and Vite only reads them from
# this folder. Nothing here is secret (they are client ids, not secrets), but
# the real .env stays gitignored anyway.
#
# Leave this file unconfigured and sign-in simply stays off — the app renders
# without a login screen, which is fine for local work against mock data.
# See SETUP-GUIDE.md Part 2 for how to create the Entra app registration.

# Directory (tenant) ID of your Entra tenant.
VITE_AAD_TENANT_ID=""

# Application (client) ID of the app registration.
VITE_AAD_CLIENT_ID=""

# The API scope you exposed on that registration.
VITE_API_SCOPE="api://<your-client-id>/access_as_user"

# Optional. Defaults to the current origin (http://localhost:5173 in dev), so
# only set this if you serve the app from somewhere else.
# VITE_AAD_REDIRECT_URI="http://localhost:5173"
